# Standalone applications

A standalone **app** is a directory of `.rocci` **modules**. Process
`@context` / `@init` occur at most once in that tree (or not at all).
`rocci run <dir>` picks the unique entry; `rocci run File.rocci` still
names the primary and loads siblings. `rocci.toml` may set `[app].entry`.
You do not write `main`. `apps.toml` is the site catalog, not a run
manifest.

Canonical source: [Counter](/examples/counter/) ·
[Counter.rocci](/examples/counter/source/Counter-rocci/).
Do not copy the file into `docs/`.

GET `/` contains `#counter`. POST increment returns a
`datastar-patch-elements` event.

This first app is **one-shot**. Increment morphs `#counter` in the acting tab
only. Shared streams are [handlers](/docs/applications/handlers/).

## State and initialization

`@context` declares the value generated `main` threads through handlers.
`@init` opens SQLite and creates the row. Failures here exit the process.
Components stay pure.

```rocci
@context { db : Sqlite.Db }

@init {
    db = Sqlite.open!(Sqlite.default_config(db_path))?
    { db: db }
}
```

## The document

`@get:view("/")` returns a full HTML document. The increment control is a
real `<button>` with an unquoted Rocci action:

```rocci
data-on:click=@post("/actions/counter/increment")
```

The card uses `id="counter"` so the later patch has a morph target.

## The one-shot patch

```rocci
@post:fragment("/actions/counter/increment") = |{ db }| {
    count = increment_count!(db)?
    counterCard({ count: count })
}
```

`?` on SQLite becomes a 500 if the query fails. There is no `@log` and no
logging from `@component`.

```sh
cargo run -q -p rocci-cli -- run \
  examples/rocci/standalone/counter --no-window --log-handlers
cargo run -q -p rocci-cli -- run \
  examples/rocci/standalone/counter/Counter.rocci --no-window --log-handlers
```

## Composition stays standalone

Split components, render lists with `@for`, variants with `@match`, and forms
without leaving generated dispatch. Point `rocci run` and
`rocci build --http-module` at the **entry** `.rocci` (the file with `@init`
and routes). Sibling `.rocci` files and authored `.roc` helpers in the
standalone tree are compiled in; do not pass a directory or a file list.
[Live counter](/examples/live-counter/) is `LiveCounter.rocci` plus
`LiveCounterUi.rocci` and `Origin.roc`. Nested apps such as
[Rocci Blocks](/examples/blocks/) put handlers in `backend/` and markup in
`ui/` behind an app-root `rocci.toml`. Custom `main.roc` is a later ownership
step, not a requirement for composition.

**Related:** [Handlers](/docs/applications/handlers/),
[Server](/docs/reference/language/server/).
